    "designNotes": "5 units with weights, topic codes/titles and class periods (full-year/semester) from the posted CED (read 2026-10-20). Six course countries: China, Iran, Mexico, Nigeria, Russia, United Kingdom. Exam: fully digital; Section I 55 MC, 60 min, 50% (40-44 individual plus 3 quantitative and 2 qualitative sets); Section II 4 FRQ, 90 min, 50% (Q1 Conceptual Analysis 4 pts/10 min, Q2 Quantitative Analysis 5 pts/20 min, Q3 Comparative Analysis 5 pts/20 min, Q4 Argument Essay 5 pts/40 min). No calculator. Skills are the CED's 1.A-5.D codes (disciplinary practices 1-5); topic-level sub-keyword skills follow the CED's suggested skill for that topic where one was read, otherwise an editorial choice. Skill weights not recorded. Per-topic and per-sub-keyword skills are an ALTON editorial mapping (one skill per sub-keyword chosen by kind and content), not the CED's per-topic suggested skills. Sub-keywords, kinds, requires and estLessons are ALTON editorial designs, not CED content. Topic titles are the CED's where read from the CED course-at-a-glance; where the extracted text was truncated they are close paraphrases."
  },
  "skills": [
    {
      "code": "1.A",
      "category": "Practice 1: Concept Application",
      "label": "Describe political systems, principles, institutions, processes, policies, and behaviors."
    },
    {
      "code": "1.B",
      "category": "Practice 1: Concept Application",
      "label": "Explain political systems, principles, institutions, processes, policies, and behaviors."
    },
    {
      "code": "1.C",
      "category": "Practice 1: Concept Application",
      "label": "Compare political systems, principles, institutions, processes, policies, and behaviors."
    },
    {
      "code": "1.D",
      "category": "Practice 1: Concept Application",
      "label": "Describe political systems, principles, institutions, processes, policies, and behaviors of a course country."
    },
    {
      "code": "1.E",
      "category": "Practice 1: Concept Application",
      "label": "Explain how political systems, principles, institutions, processes, policies, and behaviors apply in a course country."
    },
    {
      "code": "2.A",
      "category": "Practice 2: Country Comparison",
      "label": "Compare two or more course countries based on their political systems, principles, institutions, processes, policies, and behaviors."
    },
    {
      "code": "2.B",
      "category": "Practice 2: Country Comparison",
      "label": "Explain the implications of the similarities and differences between countries with similar political systems, principles, institutions, processes, policies, and behaviors."
    },
    {
      "code": "2.C",
      "category": "Practice 2: Country Comparison",
      "label": "Explain the implications of the similarities and differences between countries with different political systems, principles, institutions, processes, policies, and behaviors."
    },
    {
      "code": "3.A",
      "category": "Practice 3: Data Analysis",
      "label": "Describe the data presented."
    },
    {
      "code": "3.B",
      "category": "Practice 3: Data Analysis",
      "label": "Describe patterns and trends in data."
    },
    {
      "code": "3.C",
      "category": "Practice 3: Data Analysis",
      "label": "Explain patterns and trends in data to draw conclusions."
    },
    {
      "code": "3.D",
      "category": "Practice 3: Data Analysis",
      "label": "Explain what the data implies or illustrates about political systems, principles, institutions, processes, policies, and behaviors."
    },
    {
      "code": "3.E",
      "category": "Practice 3: Data Analysis",
      "label": "Explain possible limitations of the data provided."
    },
    {
      "code": "4.A",
      "category": "Practice 4: Source Analysis",
      "label": "Describe the author's claim(s), perspective, evidence, and reasoning."
    },
    {
      "code": "4.B",
      "category": "Practice 4: Source Analysis",
      "label": "Explain how the author's argument or perspective relates to political systems, principles, institutions, processes, policies, and behaviors."
    },
    {
      "code": "4.C",
      "category": "Practice 4: Source Analysis",
      "label": "Explain how the implications of the author's argument or perspective may affect political systems, principles, institutions, processes, policies, and behaviors."
    },
    {
